   "text": "This SMILES was read from the drawing region by region. The stereo tags are partly assumed rather than read from the wedges.\n\n**Lipid and linker (top):**\n- HOOC\u2013(CH2)16\u2013C(=O)\u2013NH is an octadecanedioic acid mono-amide. I counted 16 CH2 groups from the picture's zig-zag, which is the usual C18 diacid length.\n- It is attached to a \u03b3-Glu residue that keeps its free COOH.\n- The \u03b3-carboxyl continues through two \u2013NH\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2\u2013C(=O)\u2013 units.\n- The chain ends on the \u03b5-NH of the Lys that sits just before the Asn.\n\n**Linear peptide, read from the C-terminus:**\n- Sar-NH2, written N(C)CC(N)=O.\n- 3-pyridylalanine, then Asn, then Lys carrying the linker.\n- 4-aminotetrahydropyran-4-carboxylic acid (the spiro THP ring), then 2-naphthylalanine.\n- Tyr with an O-CH2CH2NH2 ether, then the penicillamine (Pen) that opens the ring.\n\n**Macrocycle:**\n- The top Pen is bonded through its C(CH3)2\u2013S\u2013S\u2013C(CH3)2 side chain to the lower Pen.\n- Going around the ring from the top Pen: Lys(NHAc), 7-methyl-Trp, Thr, Asn, then the lower Pen.\n\n**Exocyclic arm on the lower Pen:**\n- Lys(N\u03b1-acetyl).\n- Its \u03b5-NH carries a succinyl group (two CH2 between the carbonyls, counted from the drawing).\n- The succinyl is amide-linked to a \u03b2-amino acid bearing CH2COOH and CH2N\u207a(CH3)3.\n\n**Stereochemistry:** I could not read every wedge and hash reliably. I assigned L-configuration tags to the \u03b1-carbons and kept the Thr \u03b2-carbon as in L-Thr. The \u03b2-amino acid centre is an arbitrary guess. Some of the hashed centres in the drawing may in fact be D, so the stereo tags are the least certain part of the answer.\n\nSMILES: OC(=O)CCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCC(=O)N[C@H](C(=O)O)CCC(=O)NCCOCCOCC(=O)NCCOCCOCC(=O)NCCCC[C@H](NC(=O)C1(CCOCC1)NC(=O)[C@H](Cc1ccc2ccccc2c1)NC(=O)[C@H](Cc1ccc(OCCN)cc1)NC(=O)[C@H]3NC(=O)[C@H](CCCCNC(C)=O)NC(=O)[C@H](Cc4c[nH]c5c(C)cccc45)NC(=O)[C@H]([C@@H](C)